// Seven equal stripes, each 1/7 of the hoist, on 3:5 (the designer's 500 by 300 image).
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Gay men's pride flag, seven stripes"
  series "gay-men-pride-flag"
  version "7-stripe"
  designer "gayflagblog"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  design-rights "The designer's post says all of the flags are free to use commercially and personally, with a credit or link to the post. This file's license covers the encoding, not the design."
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20201113190641/https://gayflagblog.tumblr.com/post/186181118619/"
  source "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gay_Men_Pride_Flag.svg"
  note "The designer is the Tumblr user gayflagblog. The post read is the Wayback Machine's snapshot of 13 November 2020, which says it was edited on 30 June 2020. No earlier copy could be reached, so the date of the first post is not verified. This flag's Commons page gives 2019-10-07, and the five-stripe one's says 10 July 2019."
  note "The post gives the stripe meanings: green, Community and teal, Joy, for Nature; the white stripe is taken from the transgender flag; light blue leading into purple, Fortitude, and indigo, Diversity. It gives no hex values."
  note "The seven colors were sampled from the post's own image of this flag, a PNG, at the middle of each stripe. The stripes there are equal. The white stripe is lavender-tinted, not pure white as Commons draws it: the image draws it in two near-identical tints, #f1efff (the larger part, used here) and #efefff. Commons' other colors are within one or two units. The proportion, 3:5, is the post's own image's, 500 by 300, which Commons' drawing also has."
}
palette {
  teal "#078d70"
  light-teal "#26ceaa"
  green "#98e8c1"
  white "#f1efff"
  blue "#7bade2"
  indigo "#5049cc"
  purple "#3d1a78"
}
proportion hoist=3 fly=5

bars teal light-teal green white blue indigo purple
